## What I changed

The `GET /owners/{ownerId}` response serializes an `OwnerDto` (generated from `openapi.yml`), with MapStruct mapping fields by name from the `Owner` entity — exactly how the existing `displayName` derived field already works. So I mirrored that pattern:

1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** — added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (next to `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains an `initials` field.

2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** — added a `@Transient getInitials()`:
   ```java
   @Transient
   public String getInitials() {
       return Character.toUpperCase(this.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + "."
           + Character.toUpperCase(this.getLastName().charAt(0)) + ".";
   }
   ```

MapStruct auto-maps `getInitials()` → `OwnerDto.initials`, so no mapper or endpoint/YAML changes were needed. For `firstName="john"`, `lastName="smith"` the response now contains `"initials": "J.S."`, satisfying the new `coreComputesInitials` acceptance test.
